error[E0277]: transition body parameters do not match its input edges
  --> tests/ui/fail_inputs_without_tuple.rs:35:9
   |
31 |     b.transition(
   |       ---------- required by a bound introduced by this call
...
35 |         price,
   |         ^^^^^ this body cannot be called with what `PricingEdges<TakeEdge<Order>, SurveyEdge<Promo>>` produces
   |
   = help: the trait `TransitionBody<PricingEdges<TakeEdge<Order>, SurveyEdge<Promo>>, (PlaceRef<Order>,), _>` is not implemented for fn item `fn(Pricing) -> (Order,) {price}`
   = note: one parameter per edge, in order: `TakeEdge(p)` gives `T`, `TakeAllEdge(p)` gives `Vec<T>`, `SnapshotEdge(p)` gives `T`, `MutateEdge(p)` gives `&mut T`; a struct of edges from `#[derive(Inputs)]` gives the struct it was derived from
   = note: with `.output_distribution(f)`, the output distribution function `f` takes exactly what the body returns — the value inside the `Ok` if that is a `Result` — and returns the outputs in any form, usually a `Distribution`
   = note: a body must be `Send + Sync + 'static`: capture an `Arc`, a `Mutex` or an atomic rather than an `Rc` or a `RefCell`
